---
source: tests/cli/basics.rs
expression: help
---
fetch something once, without a project

usage: fetchloom get [options] <link>...

examples:
  fetchloom get iris
  fetchloom get https://example.org/iris.csv -o iris.csv
  fetchloom get zenodo:3608990 figshare:34744689@1 --dir downloads
  fetchloom get -i links.txt

arguments:
  [link]...  what to download: a link, a DOI, an id such as zenodo:3608990, or
             search words. several links download together, but search words go
             alone, in quotes

options:
  -o, --output <file>      write the downloaded file to <file> as it came, never
                           unpacked. needs one link to one file
      --force              replace a file already at <file> that holds other
                           bytes. it stays whole until the new file takes its
                           name
  -d, --dir <folder>       put the download in <folder> instead of a new folder
                           named after it. with several links, each gets its own
                           folder inside <folder>
  -i, --input-file <file>  read links from <file>, one per line, or from stdin
                           for -. a SHA-256 after a link checks its one file.
                           blank lines and lines starting with # are skipped
      --sha256 <hex>       check that the file has this SHA-256 before it takes
                           its name or goes in the folder. needs one link to one
                           file
      --select <glob>      keep only files matching this pattern, such as
                           "**/*.csv". repeat it for more
      --exclude <glob>     leave out files matching this pattern. repeat it for
                           more
      --no-extract         keep zip, 7z and tar archives packed instead of
                           unpacking them
  -n, --dry-run            show what would change on disk without changing it.
                           sources may still be asked what a link holds
  [global options]

on disk: writes one folder for each link, or with -o the one file it names,
through the cache. does not create data.toml or data.lock

docs: https://nikhil-yn-aix.github.io/fetchloom/user/commands/get.html
